BRANCHING SCHEME

    blr-*
        Branches not intended for upstream PRs, e.g.:

            1) blr-ci       Excessive logging
            2) blr-diary    This branch
            3) blr-scripts  My own configure/build/install/allocate scripts

    testing-*
        Branches containing a mix of PRs and blr-* branches.  For example:

            git switch commpath
            git switch -c testing-commpath
            git merge blr-ci
            git merge blr-diary
            git merge blr-scripts

        Editing occurs on (in this case) the commpath branch, which is
          then merged into testing-commpath for config/build/install/test.

        The intended benefit is getting the benefit of my ci and script
          work into the same Spindle respository without having to force
          it onto the folks working upstream.


    commpath
        Removes the "location" option and replaces it with "cachepaths"
          and "commpath".  Allows for caches to be put into a separate
          location.


    log-ts (planned)
        Add timestamps to log messages.

    dead_code_removal
        Currently a place to stash dead code removal patches as I find them.

    podman
        Scripts for doing ci in rootless containers.


