WISHLIST

    x) --logdir, change where logfiles land (will let us
        put ci logs directly on the runner's filesystem,
        rather than having to copy them out of the con-
        tainer.

    x) --logprefix, allow a user-specified tag to be
        prepended to the log filename.  Will particularly
        help in distinguishing all of the different logs
        generated by "runTests".

    x) Reformat source code using flake8 or similar.

    x) Use LC_ALL=C grep -n '[^[:print:]]' to fix debug statements that
        log unprintable text.

    x) Reconfiguring into an already-existing build directory using a
        different --rm value (e.g., flux, serial) does not update the
        existing runTests file.

    x) Go through the logs and modify and "error" messages that are
        not actually errors.

    x) Per-test timeouts, either in the testing infrastructure or
        in the ci.yml.

    x) client_recv_msg_static() and client_recv_msg_dynamic() are not
        named clearly.  The former requires a caller-allocated
        message->data buffer, the latter is callee-allocated.  Rename
        to client_recv_msg_Alloc() and client_recv_msg_NoAlloc().

    x) The above would be even clearer if the parameters were different.
        The _Alloc version should take a ldcs_message_t **, the _NoAlloc()
        version should take and ldcs_message_t *.

    x) The _NoAlloc version currently does not allow the caller to
        specify the size of the buffer being passed in.

    x) Logfiles are not creat()-ed with O_SYNC, resulting in those logfiles
        never making it to disk if a segfault comes sufficiently early.
        (Fixed.)

    x) Timestamps on log messages are occasionally useful.

